#20310
frond tri-flower stalk trumpet flower~
a tri-flower frond~
A stalk of beautiful flowers rises from the dense undergrowth.
~
The tall, deep green stalks of this plant are topped by many trumpet-shaped
flowers of vivid orange, bright yellow, and intense red. Long, pollen-covered
tendrils curl downward from the orange blossoms, wavering gently with the
slightest breeze. The yellow blossom bends over in your direction, shaking
down a heavy shower of its sticky enzyme. It looks very beautiful, but perhaps
you'd best keep your distance.
~
